! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F209E "TEST FORCED ZERO
! RESULT", sub-test E9 (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf pp.108-109,
! octal 015765.00-015770.00, the routine's own exit "BD,$+1.0").
! Six rows, and it closes out ADD DOUBLE TO MAGNITUDE: F209 is now
! transcribed end to end.
!
! Small, and the most pointed question in the whole F209E block. It
! clears LS with BLSZ, runs the E8 arithmetic again -- DLN(U) FPK38
! then D-MGA(U) FPK43, which the listing itself annotates "FORCED ZERO
! RESULT" -- and asks once, with BLS, that LS came out OFF.
!
! That makes it the oracle for the last unverified term in the model's
! double-precision LS rule:
!
!   r.ls = (res.frac == 0) && !(a.frac == 0 && b.frac == 0)
!                          && !forcedZero;
!
! F208D5 forced the res.frac term. F209D7 forced the both-zero term.
! The !forcedZero term has never been under a run: a forced zero has a
! zero result fraction, so without that term LS would come on, and
! nothing until now both produced a forced zero and asked about LS.
! E9 does exactly that, in one instruction and one question.
!
! Note what E9 is NOT: it is not a repeat of E8's fraction and sign
! checks. E8 asked what the result IS; E9 asks what the result did to
! the indicator. Same arithmetic, different question -- which is why
! it needs the BLSZ to clear LS first, and why it is the only one of
! the nine sub-tests with no CT0110 in it at all.
!
! Framework substitutes as everywhere else in this series: SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch. Constants from the
! pool p.176. PASS sits at 015770.00, on the routine's exit; the four
! rows after it (BD,$+1.0 / B,FADM4 / SIC,SENO+.32 / B,SSW) are the
! SSIP return and are not transcribed. F210 "STORE ROUNDED TEST
! ROUTINE" begins at 015772.00.
!
! Instructions: B, BLSZ, DLN(U), D-MGA(U), SIC, BLS.
! verify_fp_arith_f209e9_listing.py checks every word bit-for-bit.
!
! Observed: passes, as predicted. Dropping the !forcedZero term --
! r.ls = (res.frac == 0) && !(a.frac == 0 && b.frac == 0) -- halts E9
! with SIC storing 015770.00, the address right after its one
! BLS,SERS, while F209D6-D9 and F208D7-D11 both stay green. So E9 is
! the suite's only oracle for that term, and all three terms of the
! double-precision LS rule are now under a run.
!
! (Both were re-measured on a cleaned build tree. An earlier attempt
! reported a PASS for E9 that came from a stale simulator -- the
! give-away was the PC, 14314, which belongs to F209E5-E8 rather than
! E9's 14320. If a run's PC does not match the program's own PASS
! symbol, the binary is stale: delete bsv/build, bsv/simbuild and the
! _sim artifacts and rebuild.)

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pool p.176) --
        SLC, (8)022053.0
FPK38   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031052525252525252520
        SLC, (8)022060.0
FPK43   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031125252525252525250

! The listing prints no label at 015765.00 -- ENTRY is ours, needed
! only as the END operand. The listing's FADM4 is at 015672.00, on
! F209E1, and this routine's exit branches back to it.
! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)15765.0
ENTRY   B, $+.32                       ! F209E9: test LS ind., off condition
        BLSZ, $+.32
        DLN(U), FPK38
        D-MGA(U), FPK43                ! forced zero result
        SIC, SEN
        BLS, SERS                      ! error if LS indicator on
PASS    BEW, $                         ! 015770.00: the routine's exit ("BD,$+1.0")
        END, ENTRY
